--TEST--
An unknown member names the nearest member its own class side declares, and names nothing when the nearest one is a different word — `rule:tooling/an-agent-asks-the-binary`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A diagnostic is the documentation an agent reads after it guesses a name
// wrong, so this one carries the name it should have written. The candidates
// are what the reference could have resolved to — the same kind of member, on
// this class or on an ancestor — never a member of an unrelated class, which
// is why `refrsh` gets nothing while `Cache` declares `refresh`. And nothing
// past two edits: `disconnect` is three from `connect`, which is a different
// method rather than a slip, and an agent handed a confident wrong name will
// write it.
class Session {
    public function connect(): void {}
}
class Cache {
    public function refresh(): void {}
}
class Client extends Session {
    public function go(): void {
        self::conect();
        self::disconnect();
        self::refrsh();
    }
}
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0309]: `Client` has no method named `conect`
   --> case.nvs:18:9
   |
18 |         self::conect();
   |         ^^^^ referenced here
   = help: did you mean `connect`?

error[E0309]: `Client` has no method named `disconnect`
   --> case.nvs:19:9
   |
19 |         self::disconnect();
   |         ^^^^ referenced here

error[E0309]: `Client` has no method named `refrsh`
   --> case.nvs:20:9
   |
20 |         self::refrsh();
   |         ^^^^ referenced here

error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
